Day 31: A Heart of Sacrifice | Friday of the Fourth Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
“Take up your cross daily and follow Me.”
Not once.
Not occasionally.
Daily.

Welcome to Day 31 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection invites you into the quiet, courageous beauty of sacrifice — not suffering for its own sake, not proving your worth, not earning God’s love, but joining your heart to the heart of Christ.

This spoken‑word devotional reminds you that sacrifice is love that costs something — and because it costs something, it becomes holy. Jesus does not ask you to carry your cross alone. He carries it with you, before you, and within you.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why sacrifice is about love, not punishment

How Jesus walks with you in every cross you carry

Why small, hidden sacrifices bear real spiritual fruit

A prayer to offer your sacrifices with humility

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Jesus, let this be for love.”

